# OpenBao policy for the approle-audit AppRole — read-only visibility into
# every AppRole's own definition (secret_id TTL, redemption limit,
# source-address binding, token TTL/max TTL) so those credential-bound
# settings can be verified without a break-glass token.
#
# Deliberately a mount-wide wildcard, same reasoning as config-read: this
# grant is read/list ONLY, and every OpenBao AppRole operation that produces
# or reveals a secret_id value (minting, lookup, accessor lookup) requires
# create or update — capabilities this policy never holds. LIST on a role's
# secret-id sub-path reveals accessor IDs, never a secret_id value.
#
# State this plainly rather than softening it: GET on role-id lets a holder
# enumerate the role_id of every AppRole in the estate. A role_id is half a
# credential (see approle-issuer-policy.hcl.j2 — "role-id is a public
# identifier"), and that half is real reconnaissance value even though this
# policy cannot pair it with a secret_id to mint anything. Anyone widening
# this policy should read that sentence before adding a capability, not a
# comment that makes role-id sound inert.
path "auth/approle/role/*" {
  capabilities = ["read", "list"]
}

# Listing the mount ROOT requests `auth/approle/role` with no trailing
# segment, which the glob above does not match — without this rule the
# caller can inspect every named role but cannot enumerate what exists.
path "auth/approle/role" {
  capabilities = ["list"]
}
